## Firmographics (assumed)

| Dimension | Assumption | Confidence |
|---|---|---|
| Company type | Enterprise with a material legacy estate; Fortune 500 and upper mid-market | Medium |
| Revenue stage | $500M+ revenue, or funded scale-ups with an inherited monolith | Low |
| Geography | North America, Europe, APAC | High — matches delivery footprint |
| Industry | BFSI and Healthcare (deep practices); transport, aviation, insurance, logistics (proven) ; manufacturing (emerging) | Medium |
| Tech signal | Oracle / MSSQL / C++ / decades-old stored-procedure logic; MongoDB ecosystem; **end-of-life Realm deployments** | High — Realm is a live wedge |
| Trigger | EOL/support deadline, licensing renewal, a board mandate on AI, a failed internal AI pilot | Medium |

## Champion persona (assumed) — VP Engineering / Head of Platform

- **Owns:** the modernization roadmap and the architecture that AI initiatives will have to run on
- **Their week:** firefighting on a brittle core, defending timelines, being asked for AI outcomes the architecture cannot support
- **JTBD:** get off the legacy foundation without a disruption event that costs them their job
- **Pain, priority order:** (1) migration risk and downtime, (2) 18–36 month timelines, (3) losing context across vendor handoffs, (4) proprietary DB licensing cost
- **Decision criteria:** demonstrated zero-regression cutovers, architecture-first method, one accountable partner
- **Objection to expect:** "you're the MongoDB shop" — see `messaging.md` §7 words-to-avoid

## Economic buyer (assumed) — CTO / CIO

- **Motivation:** turn the AI mandate into business value rather than science projects; consolidate three vendors into one
- **Decision criteria:** de-risked modernization, measurable ROI, delivery accountability, Fortune 500 references
- **Frames the deal as:** capex on modernization justified by the AI outcomes it unlocks

## Anti-ICP (assumed)

- Companies wanting **staff augmentation** — bodies on a roadmap someone else owns
- **Pure greenfield** builds with no legacy estate — WeKan's core differentiator does not apply
- Buyers shopping for a **model or a chatbot** with no appetite for foundation work
- Deals scoped as **database migration only**, with no arc beyond cutover
- Organizations with **no executive mandate** for the AI transition — the program stalls at problem 1

